###Step 1: Finding the length $BC$



[[☃ image 1]]

$\begin{align}
BC^2&= {\redE{3}^2 +\redE{8}^2 } &&\text{Pythagorean theorem}
\\\\
BC&= \sqrt{\redE{3}^2 +\redE{8}^2 } &&\text{Square root both sides}
\\\\
&=\tealE{\sqrt{73}}
\end{align}$

###Step 4: Finding the perimeter

Using the lengths of all $6$ sides, we can find the perimeter of hexagon $ABCDEF$:

$\begin{align}
\text{Perimeter} &= AB+BC+CD+DE+EF+FA
\\\\
&= 11 + \tealE{\sqrt{73}}+\goldE{\sqrt{85}}+5+\goldE{\sqrt{85}}+\tealE{\sqrt{73}}
\\\\
&=16+2\sqrt{73}+2\sqrt{85}
\end{align}$
